Negative control for client-emails-filter-sort.spec.ts (AC7).

Makes the corpus resolver's collection branch ignore the request's own params and
serve all three rows unconditionally — design §7's named hazard ("the shipped
`installEmailsListHandler` ignores `request.url` entirely, so any filter/sort
assertion behind it is vacuously green") made executable. Under it, a filter that
never reached the wire would still leave the rendered rows intact, so the
narrowing and reordering assertions must go RED.

The resolver is the ONE the browser lane answers through — `recorded-corpus.ts`
is now the Playwright adapter over it (`installRecordedCorpus` →
`resolveCorpusRequest` → `servedRows`), and the force worker calls the same
function, so the mutant plants at the single seam both lanes share.

